2026-09-27T10:19:17.8976168Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8976454Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8976899Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8977337Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8977478Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8977809Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8977991Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8978247Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8978835Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8979205Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8979364Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8979784Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8980053Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8980269Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8980872Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8981413Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8982469Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8983319Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8983497Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8984266Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8985309Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8985780Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8986296Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8987008Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8987147Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8987465Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8987632Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8989940Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8992312Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8992689Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8993491Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8995626Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8996730Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8997713Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.8998448Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9099084Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9099364Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9099805Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9100091Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9102019Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9103894Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9105147Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9106517Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:17.9106872Z 
